# Held absent-site/station producer and observer Source

This is a four-file proposal only. The unsealed three-file parent draft is preserved
byte-exact; only the fourth observer file is newly adapted. No canonical file is
written, Rust source imported/executed, build/capture run, or numerical PASS claimed.
Root must first close and retain the genuine comparison failure under the current
seed-only factual checker. This proposal must not be applied before that closure.

The observer starts with constructor parameters and literal incoming site wind
owners, then uses one actual seeded EIO Vec. Site and station producers run in
Original order. `actual_return` is the parameter snapshot immediately after station
completion, before the three unchanged literal optional overrides. Its existing
`api` field identifies the final producer, `initialize_absent_weather_station`.
No case/stop/schema expansion or per-timestep manager changes are proposed.

The shared pure factory retains its final operands/equations. The genuine station
producer computes wind then temperature coefficients before EIO writes. Site
initialization retains incoming wind operands and assigns only its gradient.
Constructor coefficients 1.5863/0.0 are distinct from computed station results.
Headers and .3R/.6R operations come from the archived Original ranges and existing
Source R formatter. No Native result file or Native observed answer is used by
the preparation or proposed code.

The existing five held tests cover ordered seeded append, first-site-write failure
with station unreached, partial site row after completed header, station coefficient
assignment before its header failure, and unavailable formatting without fallback.
They remain unexecuted. Future focused selection is:
`cargo test -p ep_runtime --lib heat_balance::convection::surface_environment`.
It also selects four existing setter tests; the custody observer remains ignored.

After genuine first-failure preservation, a separately reviewed factual successor
needs only the final-producer identity and actual EIO seed-prefix/unchanged-EIO
checks across selected calls. The current comparer keeps its strict full EIO and
actual-default/preowner joins unchanged. Native constructor/input-processor owner
boundaries remain unavailable; the selected producer port does not establish
ordinary lifecycle, optional backend, or full manager compatibility.
